==Middle Dutch==

===Etymology===
Causative form of {{l|dum|clieven}}, from {{inh|dum|odt|*clievan}}, from {{inh|dum|gem-pro|*kleubaną}}. Related to {{cog|enm|cleven}} and {{cog|gmh|klieben}}.

====Verb====
{{dum-verb}}

# {{lb|dum|transitive}} to [[cleave]], to [[cut]]
#* '''c. 1475 {{CE}}''', ''Des Heiligen Cyrilli Apologi morales'';
#*:{{quote|dum|Waerom is dijn claeuwe '''geclooft'''?|Why is your claw '''cleaved'''?}}
#: {{syn|dum|schiden|clieven}}
# {{lb|dum|transitive}} to [[split]]
#: {{syn|dum|spliten|*splissen|clieven}}
# {{lb|dum|transitive}} to [[separate]]
#: {{syn|dum|scheiden|verdelen}}
# {{lb|dum|transitive}} to [[isolate]]
#: {{syn|dum|sonderen}}
# {{lb|dum|intransitive}} to [[break]], to become [[split]]
#: {{syn|dum|clieven|breken}}

